      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough sits on the east bank of the Monongahela River, where Pennsylvania Route 51 crosses the water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1803, the keelboat that launched the first stages of the Lewis and Clark Expedition was built in Elizabeth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Steamboats were built and repaired at O'Neil & Company from as early as 1895, and the Elizabeth Marine Ways operated between at least 1898 and 1925.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Old Graveyard, the borough’s oldest cemetery, is located on Bayard Street and contains burials dating back to 1774.",
